WEBVTT

0
00:00:03.619 --> 00:00:06.670
In this video we'll set up your first keypass database,

1
00:00:06.909 --> 00:00:10.350
the tool that you'll use to store every company password

2
00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:11.770
from today forward.

3
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.649
Now that you've already installed Keypass,

4
00:00:15.699 --> 00:00:17.299
when it opens for the first time,

5
00:00:17.379 --> 00:00:21.739
you're going to land on a welcome screen with no database yet like you see here.

6
00:00:21.989 --> 00:00:23.120
That's expected.

7
00:00:23.549 --> 00:00:25.639
We're going to create one from scratch.

8
00:00:27.319 --> 00:00:29.350
We'll do that by going to file

9
00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:30.899
the new database.

10
00:00:31.719 --> 00:00:34.349
When the save dialog box pops up,

11
00:00:34.729 --> 00:00:39.830
this is the single most important step in the whole video where you save this file.

12
00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:44.520
Save your database to your company managed local drive

13
00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:45.360
or

14
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.279
the IT approved corporate storage folder

15
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.319
if you'll need it in more than one device.

16
00:00:52.259 --> 00:00:54.639
Never save it to a personal Dropbox,

17
00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:56.119
Google Drive,

18
00:00:56.419 --> 00:00:57.220
iCloud,

19
00:00:57.419 --> 00:00:58.779
or personal email.

20
00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.959
That's a policy violation and puts every one

21
00:01:02.419 --> 00:01:04.599
of your company passwords at risk.

22
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:11.660
Give it a clear name so I can identify it if you ever need support.

23
00:01:12.319 --> 00:01:15.379
Try your name and company works well.

24
00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:16.980
Click save.

25
00:01:18.639 --> 00:01:20.580
Now you'll set your master password.

26
00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:22.690
This is

27
00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:25.459
the one password that protects all the others,

28
00:01:25.879 --> 00:01:27.209
so it has to be strong.

29
00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.400
Make sure it's at least 16 characters,

30
00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:32.279
a mix of uppercase,

31
00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:33.379
lowercase,

32
00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.500
numbers and symbols,

33
00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:39.319
and no dictionary words or anything tied to your personally.

34
00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:41.550
No birthdays,

35
00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:42.360
pet names,

36
00:01:42.449 --> 00:01:44.599
or reused passwords from other accounts,

37
00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:45.190
please.

38
00:01:46.559 --> 00:01:47.629
A passphrase,

39
00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:53.389
4 or 5 random unrelated words strung together is actually easier to remember

40
00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:54.949
and just as strong.

41
00:01:57.019 --> 00:01:57.540
From here,

42
00:01:57.569 --> 00:02:00.239
click OK and your database is created.

43
00:02:00.819 --> 00:02:02.980
You'll see now an empty list.

44
00:02:03.139 --> 00:02:04.080
That's normal.

45
00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:06.669
Right now,

46
00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:09.258
this is just a locked empty vault.

47
00:02:10.548 --> 00:02:13.548
In the next video you'll learn how to add your entries,

48
00:02:13.828 --> 00:02:15.628
use your entries with autotype,

49
00:02:15.828 --> 00:02:16.789
and even more.

50
00:02:17.108 --> 00:02:18.029
Thank you for joining.